            <ArticleTitle>[Dental services in bronchial asthma patients and the ways to improve them].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study was conducted in 783 bronchial asthma patients which have been established to need treatment of caries and its complications in 95.4±0.84% of cases. The received data suggest that it is possible to achieve a highly efficient treatment of caries and its complications in patients suffering from bronchial asthma in out-patient clinical conditions.</AbstractText>
